# Git remotes — GitHub primary, iConnectPlus mirror, GitLab on demand

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/ronanop/enterprise-erp.git` | **Primary** — fetch + default push |
| `iconnectplus` | `https://github.com/Moksh-CacheDigitech/iConnectPlus.git` | **Always-synced mirror** of origin |
| `gitlab` | `https://172.16.200.77/cachedigitech/cache-erp-vapt-31-aug.git` | Mirror — update only on explicit request |

GitHub `origin` is the source of truth. `iconnectplus` must stay matched to origin on every push.

Local `origin` is configured with **two push URLs** (primary + iConnectPlus), so `git push origin …` updates both. The named `iconnectplus` remote remains available for explicit sync.

## When the user asks to push / push to git

1. Push to **origin** (this also syncs iConnectPlus via the extra push URL).
2. If dual push URLs are missing or only one remote updated, also push the same ref to `iconnectplus`.
3. Do **not** push or sync GitLab unless they also asked to sync GitLab.

```bash
git push -u origin HEAD
# Fallback if iconnectplus did not update with origin:
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
```

## When the user asks to sync iconnectplus / keep iConnectPlus synced

1. Ensure local matches what should be on origin (push to `origin` first if needed).
2. Push the same refs to `iconnectplus`.

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push iconnectplus HEAD:<branch>
```

## When the user asks to sync gitlab

1. Ensure local branch matches what should be on GitHub (push to `origin` first if there are unpushed commits).
2. Push the same refs to GitLab so it matches GitHub.

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push gitlab HEAD:<branch> --force-with-lease
```

Prefer matching the current branch name on both remotes. Use `--force-with-lease` only when histories diverged and the user intends the source remote to overwrite the target.

This GitLab host uses a self-signed cert. Local repo already has `http.https://172.16.200.77/.sslVerify=false`. Auth requires a GitLab username + PAT (or SSH key); do not prompt for passwords in non-interactive sessions — ask the user for a token/URL with credentials if push fails.

## Do not

- Skip syncing `iconnectplus` when pushing to origin / "push to git"
- Auto-sync GitLab on every GitHub push
- Treat GitLab or iConnectPlus as primary fetch when the user said "push to git"
- Sync the other direction (GitLab → GitHub, or iConnectPlus → origin) unless the user explicitly asks
